 **Job Description**


Within Fugro’s flagship initiative VirGeo, we are building and delivering a geodata customer engagement platform. VirGeo is a cloud\-hosted ecosystem that lets stakeholders interact with complex geodata, monitor project progress and make informed decisions in near real\-time on survey operations. You’ll work in a multidisciplinary team that brings Product, Design and DevOps/Engineering together, so the people who shape what we build, how it looks and feels, and how it runs in production all sit around the same table.


AI\-enabled engineering is simply how we work. Our developers build alongside AI coding agents every day, we’ve invested in the instructions, skills and integrations that make those agents effective in our codebase, and we keep finding new ground. That practice only stays ahead if people keep pushing it forward, and that is a large part of this role: as a Senior Full\-stack Developer you’ll be hands\-on across the stack *and* one of the people who champions the AI mindset within the team. Developing it together with your colleagues, not for them.

**Your role**

* You design and build full\-stack web applications and platform services (React, TypeScript, Node.js, Python), with AI agents as a standard part of your toolchain;
* You build interactive map\-based tools with real\-time data integration, layer control and spatial editing, combining open\-source, proprietary and partner GIS components;
* You build and evolve the cloud\-native services that hold up at scale: multi\-tenant, resilient and cost\-aware, handling large geodata volumes and concurrent users without the experience degrading;
* You contribute to architectural decisions, work closely with Product and Design from discovery onwards and with DevOps colleagues on how what you build actually runs, and mentor other developers;
* You keep our review practice ahead of our throughput. You are accountable for everything that lands, and you’ll help evolve the review habits, tests and guardrails that make high\-velocity delivery safe;
* You keep advancing our AI\-assisted delivery practice alongside the team: decompose work into agent\-sized tasks, sharpen the context and instructions that make agents effective in our codebase, and keep human judgement where it matters — architecture, trade\-offs, security and code quality;
* You extend the shared scaffolding that makes agentic work repeatable: agent instructions, reusable skills and prompts, MCP integrations with our internal systems, automated checks and evaluation of what is actually working;
* You champion the AI mindset day to day: pair with colleagues, share what you’ve learned, challenge habits that no longer hold, and help the whole team get better.

**Your track record**

* You have a minimum of 8 years in full\-stack development, ideally in enterprise or data\-intensive environments;
* You possess deep full\-stack craft: strong front\-end skills (JavaScript/TypeScript, React or similar) and back\-end experience with Python, Java or Node.js, including API design, data modelling and service decomposition. You can reason about a whole system, not only the feature in front of you;
* You have solid experience in cloud platforms (AWS, Azure) and containerisation (Docker, Kubernetes), with real experience of what it takes to keep a service healthy in production;
* You are experienced with AI coding agents in production work (e.g. Claude Code, Cursor, GitHub Copilot), with a method behind it: context engineering, task decomposition and verifying agent output. You can talk concretely about where agents accelerate you and where they mislead you;
* You have a track record of raising the level around you: you share practice, teach by pairing, and are comfortable being challenged by colleagues who are strong in this area too;
* Ideally, you are also experienced with mapping libraries, spatial data handling and modern identity \& access management. Or the appetite to get deep into marine, offshore and remote sensing data if you haven’t worked with it before;
* You possess a strong testing discipline and healthy scepticism: the quality bar matters more, not less, when code is generated quickly;
* You are familiar with Git, CI/CD and agile ways of working;
* You have excellent communication skills and the ability to thrive in a multidisciplinary team, engaging with Product, Design and DevOps as equals rather than handing work over the wall.

**What Fugro Offers**

* A diverse and inclusive working environment;
* Based on your relevant experience, the salary ranges from €6100 to €7700\. This amount is part of our salary range, with opportunities for growth within the role;
* 29 holidays per year based on a fulltime employment (of which 4 are appointed by Fugro management) and the possibility to purchase 12 additional days;
* The opportunity to work from home in accordance with your manager and corporate policies;
* The possibility of setting up an ergonomic home office, including requesting equipment such as hardware or basic office furniture;
* Work\-from\-home allowance of EUR 2,35 net per day, where applicable;
* Commuting allowance, with mileage reimbursement for car travel (10\-30 km one\-way) and an additional EUR 0,10 per km for employees who walk or cycle to work;
* Modern pension scheme;
* Discounts on supplementary health insurance packages through Fugro’s partner providers;
* Free parking in our on\-site parking garage, with ample parking facilities and electric vehicle charging stations available;
* A bicycle leasing scheme with a company contribution;
* Possibility to register with our corporate fitness plan and access to the gym at Fugro’s headquarters, including participation in group fitness classes;
* Coaching and support through our EAP (Employee Assistance Program).

**Are you interested?**


Want to build something truly impactful, in a data\-rich professional domain, in a multidisciplinary team that is already working this way and intends to stay ahead? Apply today.


Please visit our Company Page to find out more about what it is like to work at Fugro. If you have any further questions, please contact Umit Nesar, Talent Acquisition Partner, tel. \+31 6\-81 41 07 68

**After you have applied**

* You will receive an automated confirmation email confirming receipt of your application;
* Our Talent Acquisition team (TA) will carefully review your application. If your profile matches the requirements of the role, we will contact you to discuss the next steps;
* Depending on the position, the selection process may include one or more interviews and/or assessments;
* Throughout the process, we will keep you informed about the progress;
* If, at the end of the process, there is a mutual interest from both sides, our TA team will guide you through the offer and onboarding process.
* We look forward to welcoming you to Fugro!
**Disclaimer for recruitment agencies:**

**Fugro does not accept any unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies. Acquisition to Fugro Recruitment or any Fugro employee is not appreciated**\*\*.\*\*






**For more information**
------------------------


Umit Nesar


Talent Acquisition Partner

Wat ga je doen

Als Project Engineer ben je verantwoordelijk voor het ontwerpen, implementeren en optimaliseren van moderne cloud- en werkplekomgevingen. Je vertaalt klantbehoeften naar technische oplossingen en draagt actief bij aan de verdere ontwikkeling van IT-landschappen.

Je werkt nauw samen met collega's en klanten en krijgt veel vrijheid om jouw expertise in te zetten. Daarbij denk je niet alleen mee over de techniek, maar ook over de strategie achter een oplossing.

Jouw werkzaamheden bestaan uit het:

Ontwerpen en implementeren van Azure- en Modern Workplace-oplossingen;
Uitvoeren van cloudmigraties en infrastructuurprojecten;
Adviseren van klanten over toekomstbestendige IT-oplossingen;
Signaleren van verbeterkansen binnen bestaande omgevingen;
Opstellen en uitvoeren van technische projectplannen;
Verantwoordelijkheid nemen voor een succesvolle oplevering en overdracht.

Wat breng je mee

Jij bent iemand die graag initiatief neemt en energie krijgt van complexe technische vraagstukken. Je bent nieuwsgierig naar nieuwe ontwikkelingen binnen de Microsoft-wereld en vindt het leuk om jouw kennis te delen met collega's.

Daarnaast beschik je over:

HBO werk- en denkniveau;
Ervaring als Cloud Engineer, System Engineer of vergelijkbare functie;
Kennis van Microsoft Azure en Modern Workplace;
Ervaring met hybride IT-omgevingen is een pré;
Sterke communicatieve vaardigheden en een klantgerichte instelling;
De drive om jezelf continu verder te ontwikkelen.

Waar kom je te werken

Je komt terecht bij een ambitieuze IT-dienstverlener waar innovatie, kennisdeling en persoonlijke ontwikkeling centraal staan. Samen met een team van ervaren specialisten werk je aan uitdagende cloudprojecten voor middelgrote en grotere organisaties. Van Azure-migraties tot het ontwerpen van veilige hybride omgevingen: jij bent van A tot Z betrokken.

Arbeidsvoorwaarden

Naast een uitdagende functie binnen een ambitieuze en informele IT-organisatie, kun je rekenen op uitstekende arbeidsvoorwaarden:

Een bruto maandsalaris tussen €4.500 en €6.000, afhankelijk van jouw kennis en ervaring;
Een dienstverband van 32 tot 40 uur per week, afgestemd op jouw wensen;
Een elektrische leaseauto en de mogelijkheid gebruik te maken van een aantrekkelijk fietsleaseplan;
27 vakantiedagen om voldoende tijd te hebben voor ontspanning en opladen;
Een onbeperkt opleidingsbudget voor trainingen, cursussen en persoonlijke ontwikkeling;
Volop mogelijkheden om Microsoft-certificeringen te behalen en je technische kennis verder uit te breiden;
Een maandelijkse thuiswerkvergoeding en telefoonvergoeding;
De keuze tussen een Microsoft- of Apple-laptop;
Een volledig betaalde basispensioenregeling met de mogelijkheid deze verder uit te breiden;
Flexibele werktijden en de mogelijkheid om hybride te werken;
Een verzorgde lunch op kantoor en dagelijks vers fruit;

